From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:55:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 007/117] clk: apple: add T8010 touch clock driver

The J172 touch controller needs a 24 MHz platform clock generated by a
small divider block inside T8010 PMGR.  The block has separate disable and
enable controls, reports a busy transition, and encodes divider 1024 as
zero in its 10-bit divider field.

Add a clock provider that programs the divider, sequences the gate around
PMGR busy polling and reports the effective rate.  Keep this separate from
the SPI and Z2 protocol drivers so those consumers only use the common
clock API.

The disable callback may run in atomic context, so retain the required
100 us hardware settling delay as udelay().  Register the driver and its
binding in MAINTAINERS with this commit.

The object and J172 DT were built with LLVM 18.  The complete series passed
a fresh J172 boot and the DT620 single- and multi-touch test.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 37a9f79506ed1c58d2cea8d96e26137c24b9652d
